  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0-preview.5\n\n\t\t=== Generative UI Level 2 - cards ===========================================\n\t\t- NEW - a tool can return MentorCard (or several) instead of a string and the widget renders a real card: title, subtitle, label/value fields, an accent colour and buttons. Level 1 was Markdown the model wrote; this is structure your code returns, so the model only chooses when to call the tool.\n\t\t- Because the card comes from application code and not from the model, it can safely carry actions: nothing said in the conversation can add a button or change where one points. Buttons send a message, navigate, or run a page-registered UI action.\n\t\t- The model is told the card is already on screen and receives the data in compact form, so it comments on it instead of repeating every field as a table underneath.\n\t\t- EnableGenerativeCards (default true) turns rendering off and falls back to the previous text behaviour.\n\t\t- Tool results are marshalled through JSON by the function factory, so cards are recognised structurally rather than by CLR type; ordinary tool results are deliberately not mistaken for cards.\n\n\t\t=== Declarative agents ======================================================\n\t\t- NEW - IMentorAgentSource: supply Level-2 specialists that the [MentorAgent] attribute scan cannot see. They join the same handoff graph, so route_to_specialist reaches them identically. The tools handed to a source arrive already wrapped in the gate, so role checks and human approval keep working inside an agent's own function-calling loop.\n\t\t- The MentorAgent.Declarative package builds such agents from YAML files.\n\n\t\t=== Voice ===================================================================\n\t\t- CHANGED - voice output now speaks each sentence as the answer streams, instead of reading the finished reply back. Previously the assistant stayed silent for the whole response and then recited it.\n\t\t- NEW - VoiceBargeIn (default true): playback stops when the user presses the microphone, sends a message, presses Stop or starts a new conversation.\n\t\t- NEW - VoiceHandsFree (opt-in): the transcript is sent on silence and the microphone reopens once the spoken answer ends. It is held shut while the assistant speaks, so it does not transcribe the assistant.\n\t\t- NEW - VoiceStreaming, VoiceRate.\n\n\t\t=== Onboarding tour =========================================================\n\t\t- NEW - EnableOnboardingTour: a short guided tour on a user's first open of the widget, generated from the pages registered with [MentorPage] and the assistant's own tools, so it cannot describe a screen that no longer exists. Each step can carry a ready-made question the user sends in one tap.\n\t\t- Generated once per process and shared by every visitor. A generated URL matching no registered page is dropped rather than shown. With no ChatClient it falls back to a deterministic tour built from the same data.\n\t\t- Register your own IMentorTour to script the tour by hand.",
